WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Orion Worktree Report observes the
local repositories you

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.420
select. In this disposable example,
the first scan

3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.660
observes three registered worktrees
and reports no uncommitted

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.440
path overlap.

5
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.280
Now two worktrees change the same
tracked path.

6
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.080
The scan reports the shared path and
exits

7
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:18.440
one, with complete coverage.

8
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.600
It observes this overlap without
deciding which worker

9
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.240
should proceed.

10
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.760
Add an unavailable repository and
coverage becomes partial.

11
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.940
The known overlap stays visible,
while the total

12
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.380
is unknown. This report grants no
task ownership,

13
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.420
file lock or merge permission.

14
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.040
The source and walkthrough are
linked below.
